{
  "dom_id": "step-18447",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Quadratic Trinomials With Leading Coefficients",
  "problem": "Factor $2p^4 + 5p^2 + 3.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $t = p^2$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{p}^{4}+5{p}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ 2{({p}^{2})}^{2}+5{p}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+5t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+5t+3 & = \\\\ (t+1)(2t+3) & = \\\\ ({p}^{2}+1)(2{p}^{2}+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
